The embedded diffuse Milky Way is adapted from Deep Star Maps 2020:
https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/4851/
Sources: milkyway_2020_4k.exr (texture), starmap_2020_4k.exr (photometric
reference), both in celestial ICRF/J2000 coordinates.
Credit: NASA/Goddard Space Flight Center Scientific Visualization Studio.
Gaia DR2: ESA/Gaia/DPAC.
Visualization by Ernie Wright (USRA).

Adaptations: linear-light reduction to 1024x512, sRGB encoding and lossy WebP
compression; empirical normalization from unsaturated catalogue stars.
No constellation figures or boundaries are included.
NASA media usage guidelines: https://www.nasa.gov/nasa-brand-center/images-and-media/
Gaia credit: https://gea.esac.esa.int/archive/documentation/GDR2/Miscellaneous/sec_credit_and_citation_instructions/

The embedded point-star dataset is derived from the HYG Stellar Database v4.1,
Copyright David Nash / Astronexus. It is licensed under Creative Commons
Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0):
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/
Source: https://github.com/astronexus/HYG-Database
Revision: c7f7f883fe678cc7680169a50ccd7dcc49b060ce
Data: hyg/CURRENT/hygdata_v41.csv

Adaptations: select V <= 6.5; convert J2000 positions/proper motions and
V magnitudes/B-V colours to GPU point records; compress the
result as star-catalog.bin.gz. This adapted dataset retains CC BY-SA 4.0.
The library code is a separate work and retains the project's MIT license.

Photometric filter response: SVO Filter Profile Service, Generic/Johnson.V
https://svo2.cab.inta-csic.es/theory/fps/fps.php?ID=Generic/Johnson.V

Lunar orbital elements and main perturbation formulae: Paul Schlyter,
"How to compute planetary positions": https://stjarnhimlen.se/comp/ppcomp.html
Lunar visual phase-law reference: Krisciunas & Schaefer (1991),
"A Model of the Brightness of Moonlight", PASP 103, 1033.
Natural moonless-night horizontal illuminance reference (0.8 millilux):
U.S. National Park Service, "Metrics Guide to Night Skies Report":
https://www.nps.gov/subjects/nightskies/NSQmetrics.html
